ShellacFilters use framework from Airwindows (MIT licensed).

Declick and dehum had been trained on various shelllac transfers, including those from tangotunes.com and tangotimetravel.be

Dehum was inspired by loud noise around 40Hz in several transfers, primarily by Cachirulo and Tablada. TT transfers were compared with TTT which have no low frequency noise.

The idea of Declick came after a super clean transfer from original metal master disc was released: https://tangotimetravel.be/product/malvon/

I don't release VST filters because specialized plugins (foobar2000, VirtualDJ, etc) are able to scan files entirely. The filters are also integrated in https://github.com/shaforostoff/EmbraceNG and https://github.com/richardsladetdj-creator/TangoDisplay
If you would like them to be integrated into you favourite player (and it is either open source, or supports plugins) - feel free to ask me: https://www.facebook.com/shaforostoff
